WEBVTT

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:09.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the first of October. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:16.300
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, got you. Unlike the heating in the portakabin, which has apparently decided not to join us.</v>

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:20.329
<v Fiona Doyle>You've still got your coat on, then?</v>

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:28.960
<v Marcus Hale>Never mind that, whose is the new car in the car park? Takes up about a bay and a half.</v>

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.700
<v Hannah Price>That's the parking, not the car.</v>

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.229
<v Marcus Hale>Ah, right. Operator error. Familiar story.</v>

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:44.079
<v Olumide Adeyemi>While we're on important matters, the charity bake sale on Friday. Apparently there's proper cake this time.</v>

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.450
<v Aisha Begum>What was wrong with the last lot?</v>

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.579
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nothing, if you needed a wheel chock.</v>

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:56.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes evidence against somebody's baking. Finished bits first, please.</v>

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:02.530
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, already swapped the filter on the dryer yesterday. That's done, not something for today's list.</v>

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.659
<v Fiona Doyle>That's the filter change closed, then?</v>

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.319
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, finished yesterday.</v>

00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:17.870
<v Hannah Price>And I already swapped the filter on the line two yesterday. Same thing, completed work, just feeding it back.</v>

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.060
<v Aisha Begum>Right, yeah. I had that down as yesterday's as well.</v>

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:29.060
<v Priya Raman>Also, tested the line 2 robot yesterday and it's all fine now. No follow-on job from that.</v>

00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:32.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Those are all closed, not being rolled over.</v>

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:41.170
<v Priya Raman>One observation, though. Heard a slight rattle from the Forklift Fleet, nothing to action yet. Just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only, no new job off that.</v>

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:55.640
<v Aisha Begum>Same sort of thing from me. Saw the pressure on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:01.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>It recovered completely, did it? Sorry, talked over the last bit.</v>

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:08.189
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, back on its own. Nothing I'm asking anyone to do from that, just the observation.</v>

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:12.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Actual work to agree, then.</v>

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:17.280
<v Marcus Hale>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the BFP.</v>

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.030
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marc. That's top priority please.</v>

00:02:21.449 --> 00:02:24.599
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll treat the BFP sign-off as top priority.</v>

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.180
<v Priya Raman>Just so we're clear, you mean the lock-out tag-out sign-off itself?</v>

00:02:31.789 --> 00:02:35.990
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, exactly that. Not saying it's signed off already; I'll do it.</v>

00:02:36.979 --> 00:02:38.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Marc has that one.</v>

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:46.500
<v Fiona Doyle>There's still the purchase order for the dryer as well. Separate from the filter that's already done.</v>

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:54.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi, can you chase the purchase order for the dryer by the end of the week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:56.699 --> 00:03:01.949
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the dryer by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:06.889
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, the filter— sorry, you've already said it. Different thing.</v>

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.289
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep. Nobody's asking you to swap it twice.</v>

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:18.969
<v Sarah Okafor>And Fi, just to keep the weighting clear, it matters but it's not urgent. End of the week is what we're agreeing.</v>

00:03:20.889 --> 00:03:22.990
<v Fiona Doyle>Understood. That's mine, on that basis.</v>

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:29.530
<v Aisha Begum>What about the guarding on the line 2 guard? That's the other item, isn't it?</v>

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:36.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. I'll check the guarding on the line 2 guard on the 3rd. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.080
<v Fiona Doyle>On the 3rd, which is Saturday. That's deliberate, yeah?</v>

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:46.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, on the 3rd. Not moving it to tomorrow.</v>

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.889
<v Hannah Price>Okay, Saz has the line 2 guard check on the 3rd, fairly important.</v>

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.250
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, I'll do that.</v>

00:03:55.479 --> 00:03:59.330
<v Fiona Doyle>And the pre-use checks on the forklifts? Separate entry from that.</v>

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:07.069
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll do the pre-use checks on the forklifts next Tuesday. That's fairly important as well.</v>

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:12.189
<v Fiona Doyle>Got you. Sarah Okafor against the forklifts pre-use checks, next Tuesday.</v>

00:04:13.949 --> 00:04:16.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's mine. Next Tuesday, fairly important.</v>

00:04:17.009 --> 00:04:21.910
<v Priya Raman>And that's the planned pre-use checks, not a new investigation from my rattle comment?</v>

00:04:22.939 --> 00:04:25.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Your observation hasn't created another task.</v>

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:34.259
<v Priya Raman>Um, before we get onto the Stretch Wrapper, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Stretch Wrapper.</v>

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.240
<v Fiona Doyle>So that delivery-dependent bit is still blocked, not something we're promising today.</v>

00:04:42.339 --> 00:04:46.889
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Still no confirmation. That's a blocker update, not me adding a chase.</v>

00:04:48.709 --> 00:04:58.160
<v Marcus Hale>The existing jam is separate from that delivery, though. I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Stretch Wrapper by the end of the week.</v>

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:05.269
<v Aisha Begum>Right, the jam and the sensors, not taking on the supplier delivery as well?</v>

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:10.899
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, just the jam and sensor check. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:21.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Marc, clear the jam and check the sensors on the Stretch Wrapper by the end of the week. It matters but it's not urgent, agreed.</v>

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.379
<v Marcus Hale>Agreed, I'll do that. Separate from the blocked delivery.</v>

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:32.779
<v Fiona Doyle>That's clear now. The work Marc's taken isn't dependent on that delivery; the delivery-dependent work stays blocked.</v>

00:05:33.089 --> 00:05:36.589
<v Priya Raman>Yep. No extra supplier job coming out of my update.</v>

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:43.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. That's the distinction I wanted. No accidental extras on the list.</v>

00:05:43.689 --> 00:05:47.540
<v Hannah Price>Nothing else from quality. Mine was just the completed filter change.</v>

00:05:47.939 --> 00:05:54.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nothing else from me either. Except I feel the wheel-chock cake comment may come back to haunt me.</v>

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.110
<v Aisha Begum>You're on Teams. There's witnesses.</v>

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Plenty of them. Right, we're agreed. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.670
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.259
<v Priya Raman>Cheers.</v>
